<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43137" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">scrūtārĭus</span></b> ,
			a, um
		scruta. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			Adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to trash</i>, <i>frippery</i>, or <i>trumpery</i>: SERVVS, perh. <i>a
				dealer in such things</i>, <i><span class="en">Inscr. Orell.
				2954</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			Subst. * </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">scrū-tārĭus</span></b> ,
			ii, m., <i>a dealer in
				second-hand clothes</i>, <i>a broker</i>, <i>ragman</i>, Lucil. ap. <i><span class="en">Gell. 3,
				14, 10</span></i> (v. scruta).—* </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">scrūtārĭa</span></b> ,
			ae, f., <i>the business of
			a</i> scrutarius, <i><span class="en">App. M. 4, p. 146,
			17</span></i>.—* </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>C.</b> ‡ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">scrūtārĭum</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γρυτοπωλεῖον,</span> Gloss. Gr. Lat.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
